      ],
      "statement": "Writing a=κ^e and P_e=P/(T−a), the product β=∏ᵢγ^(−i)(α)^{[Tⁱ]P_e} realizes the divisor prescribed in the single weight-one block at t₀. The gluing maps carry determinant one on every other block and slope.",
      "hypotheses": "Work with the cyclic layer and allowed divisor of DET-01. The supplied Steinitz lattice isomorphism theorem is applied fiber by fiber after the Galois relabeling for t₀. In weight one the coordinate (1,0) gives a nonempty fiber.",
      "definitions": [
        "twisted principal divisor",
        "Galois action on primes",
        "block determinant",
        "Steinitz isomorphism"
      ],
      "correspondence": "Inverse conjugation on α yields a positive shift on the divisor index. Convolution with T−a turns the coefficients of P_e into the coefficients of P. The same γ^(−i) identifies weight κⁱ with 1 before the blocks are assembled.",
