      "statement": "After normalization by n_{t₀}^{−1}, the conjugate block contributions give P_e(a) times the residue index of N_a(α).",
      "hypotheses": "At a tested degree-one prime 𝔭 of F away from ℓB, k=𝒪_F/𝔭 and f(z)=v(z mod 𝔭). Its domain here is the Galois-stable subgroup of z∈F× with order zero at every finite prime of F not dividing B𝒪_F, for the chosen B∈𝒪_{L′}∖{0}. All scalar identities are in ℤ/q.",
      "definitions": [
        "cyclotomic action on μ_q",
        "residue index",
